# Project Context

Full-stack K2 printer analytics platform with:
- Backend: FastAPI (Python), PostgreSQL, async Moonraker polling
- Frontend: React + Vite + TypeScript, TailwindCSS
- Monitoring: Grafana dashboards, Prometheus scraping
- Auth: JWT with 7-day tokens, SHA256+salt password hashing

## Key Conventions

- PrintStatus enum UPPERCASE: COMPLETE, CANCELLED, PRINTING, FAILED
- Use `datetime.now(timezone.utc)` NOT `datetime.utcnow()`
- No `depends_on: moonraker` in docker-compose.yml
- Moonraker at 192.168.1.146:7125
- Power rate: $0.49/kWh AUD, TZ: Australia/Perth
- Backend Dockerfile: no `--reload` flag
- Frontend: Vite dev server on port 3000, proxies `/api` → backend:8000

## Code Style

- NO comments in code unless absolutely necessary
- Concise, direct responses
- Mimic existing code style and patterns
- Use existing libraries, don't add new ones without checking
- Never add emojis unless asked

## Workflow

- Before making changes, understand the codebase structure
- After changes, run lint/typecheck if available
- Verify with tests when possible (23 debug tests available)
- Never commit unless explicitly asked
- Add session context to AGENTS.md or SESSION.md as we work

## Filament & CFS

- CFS slot ID is positional (T1A), not physical spool
- measuring_wheel is per-TRAY, NOT per-slot
- Use `cfs_slot_overrides.remaining_pct` as authoritative (not CFS remain_len)
- RFID vendor provides unique spool identity when available
- Color hex codes stored with `#` prefix, normalized to 6 chars
- Spool change detection: color_hex + rfid_vendor mismatch

## Deployment

- Deploy: tar + ssh to Proxmox CT 104 at 192.168.1.203
- DB: PostgreSQL k2user:k2pass@db:5432/k2_analytics
- Container rebuild: docker compose up -d --build
